WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.490 --> 00:00:07.589
Continue working on your project or re-open the one context project from the last video.

2
00:00:08.439 --> 00:00:15.580
At this stage, you see the architectural model in the scene and nothing else except for a generic ground and a background.

3
00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:20.219
We'll be setting this project in France, in Paris to be precise.

4
00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:24.219
Under Populate in the Dock, choose the Urban panel.

5
00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:31.309
If you zoom out, you'll notice that they are viewing an area of Paris, France.

6
00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:38.020
Twinmotion was originally developed in France, so this is a bit of an homage to that.

7
00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:44.820
This spot will work for us, but you can obviously pick a spot anywhere in the world using the map or the search box.

8
00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:56.899
Zoom on an area around the Ile de la Cité where the famous Notre Dame Basilica is set, and grab that area by clicking the Download button.

9
00:00:57.939 --> 00:01:04.579
This will take a moment as the system fetches information from OpenStreetMap and places the data around your project.

10
00:01:08.659 --> 00:01:17.500
Once done, look at the scene graph and note how the project and the surroundings are set under two different containers for easier selection.

11
00:01:18.739 --> 00:01:24.019
This means you can easily control the visibility of the environment and the architectural project separately.

12
00:01:25.219 --> 00:01:32.459
Hierarchies are preserved, which means that you can select the top parents to adjust and place assemblies appropriately.

13
00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:39.390
Select and move a few of these trees to make place for the project.

14
00:01:47.599 --> 00:01:49.500
Place the project appropriately.

15
00:01:56.939 --> 00:01:59.099
There are a few other things that you can do.

16
00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:05.239
For example, the current background shows a city that looks more North American than European.

17
00:02:06.409 --> 00:02:10.650
You can change that in the Ambient panel, under the Horizon section.

18
00:02:14.539 --> 00:02:20.719
Let's use a European city instead. You can also adjust the rotation as you see fit.

19
00:02:26.909 --> 00:02:38.620
Since we're dealing with global adjustments, let's set the time of day to about 4.30pm, and the North offset to about 65 degrees.

20
00:02:40.669 --> 00:02:46.169
As a bonus, and since we are on an island, let's bring some water in.

21
00:02:47.379 --> 00:02:51.479
In the scene graph, make sure to hide the generic starting ground.

22
00:02:55.490 --> 00:02:59.129
In the Ambience panel, enable Ocean mode.

23
00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:06.939
Set the height so that it is below the ground. Minus 100cm should be enough.

24
00:03:14.870 --> 00:03:16.830
Choose a water aspect that you like.

25
00:03:26.009 --> 00:03:30.150
I admit I like the default Clear River best, so I'll keep that one.

26
00:03:30.150 --> 00:03:38.000
Save your work. Next, we work on embellishing the architectural project with the help of ready-made materials.
